<li><a href=3D"https://www.linkedin.com/company/anthropicresearch/" data-at=
tribute-index=3D"0" data-entity-type=3D"MINI_COMPANY">Anthropic</a> claims =
that its latest GenAI app, Opus, =E2=80=9Cexhibits near-human level of comp=
rehension and fluency on complex tasks=E2=80=A6=E2=80=9D Really? So, let=E2=
=80=99s take a closer look at what Anthropic <em>really</em>&nbsp;says abou=
t its app. We start by looking at their terms and conditions of service. In=
 relevant part we find the following:YOUR USE OF THE SERVICES AND MATERIALS=
 IS SOLELY AT YOUR OWN RISK. THE SERVICES AND OUTPUTS ARE PROVIDED ON AN =
=E2=80=9CAS IS=E2=80=9D AND =E2=80=9CAS AVAILABLE=E2=80=9D BASIS AND, TO TH=
E FULLEST EXTENT PERMISSIBLE UNDER APPLICABLE LAW, ARE PROVIDED WITHOUT WAR=
RANTIES OF ANY KIND, WHETHER EXPRESS, IMPLIED, OR STATUTORY.Forget all the =
claims you read earlier. Those were just meant to get your attention and su=
bscribe to the service. What really matters and what Anthropic is really sa=
ying is that your use of Opus is at your own risk, it doesn=E2=80=99t stand=
